  "contentHtml": "<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/6e143325-c7c7-37f3-3355-975fc53161bb.png\" width=\"628\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span>Hey Brew Shop Fam!<br>Here's an update of what's happening this week - from new&nbsp;beer drops, wine reviews, our current tap list, to upcoming tastings, and more.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<a href=\"https://arlbrew.us16.list-manage.com/track/click?u=be20bbfba341582993786f7f0&amp;id=de5c1b5b83&amp;e=01c6cdb4b7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SHOP THIS WEEK’S NEWSLETTER HERE</a>\n<a href=\"https://arlbrew.us16.list-manage.com/track/click?u=be20bbfba341582993786f7f0&amp;id=d240ab798b&amp;e=01c6cdb4b7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SHOP OUR ENTIRE STOCK OF BEER, WINE &amp; HOMEBREW HERE</a>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/2983dc84-db51-f35d-9fd6-f60e96578556.png\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span><span>Join us this</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Friday from 5-7 PM</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> as we welcome Jon from</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;Afterglow&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>for our free tasting! Scroll down to the bottom of our newsletter to see the full August line-up!</span></span></span></span></p>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/76076ccd-6fad-4097-6722-74ed5241a370.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🌊 Fresh from VA Beach </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Commonwealth</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Luftschloss</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Kellerbier<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Triumph</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> West Coast IPA with Triumph &amp; Cryo Cascade<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Tiki Townie </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Gose with Coconut, Banana, Strawberry, Mango, Orange &amp; Vanilla</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/a1487cde-5cbd-7715-50b7-88759378f1ee.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍃 Fresh </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Veil </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>hops<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Haze Between</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Blue Ferrari </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Hazy DIPA with Amarillo &amp; Galaxy<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Dirt Dirt Nap Nap</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy DDH DIPA with Galaxy, Citra, Mosaic &amp; Nelson Sauvin</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/f833cabb-fc07-440f-91bb-2c65964d90f4.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f5e1_fe0f/72.png\" alt=\"🗡️\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></span></span></span><span> Sacrifice nothing with </span></span><strong><span><span>Adroit Theory</span></span></strong><span><span><br>• </span></span><strong><span><span>Sacrifice of the Damned</span></span></strong><span><span> Hazy DIPA with Citra, Motueka &amp; Riwaka<br>• </span></span><strong><span><span>BLVCK Celebration</span></span></strong><span><span> Imperial Porter with Molasses, Maple Syrup &amp; Black Lava Salt<br>• </span></span><strong><span><span>AK [Silent Warrior]</span></span></strong><span><span> Hazy Triple IPA with Citra, Galaxy, Nelson Sauvin &amp; El Dorado</span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d6e2f66d-6fee-5b72-8d1f-4b08c71c9c00.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p>💭 Fresh <strong>Other Half </strong>drop!</p>\n<p>• <strong>Oh...toberfest</strong>&nbsp;Marzen</p>\n<p>• <strong>Superfun!</strong> Session Hazy IPA with Galaxy, Simcoe &amp; El Dorado</p>\n<p>•<strong> Terp Mart</strong> Hazy IPA with Citra, Citra Cryo, Rakau &amp; Nelson Sauvin</p>\n<p>• <strong>Daydreamless </strong>Hazy DIPA with Citra, Mosaic, Amarillo, Cashmere, Citra Cryo &amp; Mosaic Cryo</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/8b4e118c-1925-9b10-a366-03a4034a82f9.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>👊 Two Local Powerhouses for the Wheat door<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ardent Saison</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Port City Wit Ferrari</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> hoppy witbier - collab with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>The Veil</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/741a7eea-073d-efc3-0c55-5e3b0539d198.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍁 Malt Heads Unite!<br> • </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Allagash Foliage Report </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Belgian Dubbel<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>New Belgium Fat Tire Classic Recipe</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Amber Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Great Lakes Nosferatu</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Double Red IPA</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/6cd0074f-b309-c85e-d175-6c35b86016c5.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🐢 All the best juice<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Coastal Ecliptic Mosaic</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Eclipse &amp; Mosaic - collab with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Final Gravity</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Coastal Sea Turtles Rule</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Citra, Sabro &amp; Motueka<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Afterglow Mother Fluffer </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Sour with Peach, Pineapple &amp; Marshmallow</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/257c828a-3627-1348-8378-82c0535742af.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🤝Pucker up with </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Crooked Run</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Waverunner </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Sour with Tangerine, Passionfruit &amp; Pineapple<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Stuck Together</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Sour with Mango, Coconut &amp; Rice Milk</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/4fc3f5f7-afe6-97dc-bfa4-3f088733ed3d.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🥨 Fall Ready!<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Sixpoint Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Bingo Beer Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Jack’s Abby Copper Legend</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Festbier<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Destihl Oktoberfest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Marzen<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Brooklyn Oktoberfest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Marzen</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/13fc8f73-82f6-1f16-1bc4-ff524248be58.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>❤️ Local love from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Aslin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Chirp </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Hazy IPA with Citra &amp; Amarillo<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Bringing Extra Sexy Back </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Hazy DIPA with Mosaic</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/b2dd00c5-c1bd-ab86-2caf-226b34f9921c.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🎃 Heavy hitter seasonals from </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Southern Tier</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pumqueen</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pumpkin Cider<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Pumking</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Pumpkin Ale<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Maple Warlock</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Pumpkin Stout with Maple</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/e056ac7d-b6ee-8de6-c4c6-54a00aa7e0ed.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍺 Moar Oktoberfest<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Hacker Pschorr Oktoberfest </span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Ayinger Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Avery The Kaiser</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Oktoberfest Marzen<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Bell’s Octoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Marzen</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/cea5d234-f68d-107f-3a42-deb932fada56.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🎃 Pumpkin, pumpkin!<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Schlafly Vanilla Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Brooklyn Post Road Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>1911 Haunted Hayride</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Pumpkin Cider</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/c3ac84da-764d-6c76-63ac-210109570888.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>👻 Moar pumpkin<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Dogfish Head Punkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Flying Dog The Fear</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> New Belgium Atomic Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Athletic Dark &amp; Gourdy</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Non-Alcoholic Pumpkin</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/0f5d04f4-10af-052a-831b-47903850ad56.jpeg\" width=\"628\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>🍂You guys, it's fall</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Starr Hill Festie</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Oktoberfest Marzen</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Heavy Seas Greater Pumpkin</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Bourbon Barrel Aged Pumpkin Ale</span></span></span></p>\n<p>Bluejacket / Schilling / Eggenberg Artus Vienna Lager</p>\n<p>COTU Oktoberfest</p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/e4e22b77-6230-c8a4-a129-d865642c14e6.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Le Facteur Vouvray Brut Nature NV</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span><span><span><span>The Loire brings us lots of things to love but one of the more under-the-radar things is Sparkling Chenin Blanc. Traditional method and zero dosage means you're getting a wonderfully dry sparkler here. Notes of pear, citrus, and minerality, with fine bubbles and lively acidity. Certified Organic.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Castellano Pinot Grigio</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span><span><span><span>We're always on the hunt for affordable, easy drinking and tasty Pinot Grigio. Castellano nails it with this adorable bottle. Fresh green apple and pear plus zippy acidity.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span>Domaine de Sulauze Coteaux d'Aix-en-Provence Rose \"Pompenette\": </span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Provence Rose at its finest, Pomponette is that classic pale pink crispy beauty you know you love. Gorgeous aromatics lead the way for this bright, easy drinking Rose. Notes of watermelon and a fresh strawberry field pair with zippy acidity and lovely minerality. Certified Organic &amp; Biodynamic.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Patricia Green Dollar Bills Only Pinot Noir:</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Patricia Green Cellars unapologetically prides itself in producing more individual bottlings of Pinot Noir than any other winery in America. Lumpy's is an iconic dive bar in the Willamette Valley that houses a charming jukebox nicknamed \"Dollar Bills Only.\" The nickname pays homage to making the best of bad situations and, well, Patricia Green Cellars released the first (and supposedly only) vintage of DBO in 2020 when everything went to shit. Never say never. Dollar Bills Only is back for a welcome reboot - silky and elegant but also light-hearted and fun to drink with notes of raspberry, rose petal and orange peel.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Le Vignerons Du Castelas Tranquille Pinard: </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>Our eyes lit up when we sipped this patio ready Rhone blend. Coming from organic clay and limestone vineyards, the wine undergoes a five-week skin contact maceration before aging in concrete - resulting in a fresh, crunchy, low-tannin profile that is best enjoyed slightly chilled with a nose of juicy raspberry and cherry and a light, fruit-forward palate. Organic.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Boyer de Bar Bourgogne Rouge:</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>We love when friendship and business collide. Vincent Boyer and Emmanuel Lucas de Bar met in winemaking school and each launched incredible careers in Burgundy. They've joined forces with the mission to make affordable, delicious wines from organically grown fruit in Burgundy (read as: grand cru treatment without the grand cru price tag). The result is everything a great village Burgundy should be: translucent ruby in the glass with red cherry, raspberry, subtle earth and a silky palate of bright red fruit, forest floor and an elegant finish. Organic, Native Yeast &amp; Hand Harvested</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Panas Red Agiorgitiko:</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>The second Agiorgitiko (ah-your-yeek-tee-ko) to grace our shelves - it's the most widely planted red grape in Greece and you all can't get enough. Fresh fruit of plum and dark cherry with plenty of spice and earthiness, plus a kiss of grippy tannins.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/7ab07e35-caa0-a78b-1d07-f0b3b0945a2b.jpeg\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>This summer I've been given an enormous gift. My neighbor, Sara, drives my son each morning to camp where she's a counselor at an adjacent camp at the same school. Instead of spending my mornings trying to figure out how to be in two places at one time, I have an extra second for myself and a cup of hot coffee. I've been neighbors with Sara for 14 years — I still remember her and her brother peering through the windows on the day we moved in — and now she's a college graduate just learning about wine. As a small thank you, I've had an absolute blast bringing Sara bottles of wine every Friday this summer. I've included many fan favorites: Early Mountain Rose, Mary Taylor Veneto, Joseph Cattin Cremant d'Alsace and this week I'm bringing </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Zlatan Dalmatia Marina \"Bilo Idro.\"</span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span><span><span>The end of summer is just screaming for coastal wine so we're heading to the island of Havar off the Dalmatian Coast. Zlatan Plenković started out as a humble fisherman on the island before he founded Croatia's second-every private winery in 1991 — the same year Croatia declared independence from Yugoslavia. Zlatan built his cellar from limestone boulders dug right out of the cliffs above the Adriatic Sea. As you can imagine, the terrain is rugged with the vines planted into the side of a mountain at 10-20 percent inclines secured only by rocky soil. Marina \"Bilo Idoro\" is a mineral-driven field blend of all indigenous Croatian varietals — Bogdanuša, Pošip, Maraština, Prč, Trebbiano Toscana to name just a few &nbsp;— with each fermenting separately before blending. The result is a stunning combo of peach and citrus paired with sea-inspired salinity. Zippy, refreshing and whimsical enough to transport you to a seat at </span><span>Zlatan's marina side restaurant Bilo Idro. Pair with chilled seafood, crispy salads and the great outdoors with your neighbors. </span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span><br>If you were worried, Sara and Sam also get their caffeine (or cake pop) fix on their \"Starbucks Fridays.\" I'll be sad to see this summer go for a number of reasons, but a big one will be missing Sam's send off each morning with Sara and the sound of Pink Pony Club on repeat. </span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Beth</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/ee114eb5-8f0d-9c75-610a-7cf185e13f8a.png\" width=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
